						},
						{
									"@type": "HowToStep",
									"position": 2,
									"name": "Check the micron range",
									"text": "Each method shows the target particle size range in microns. For example, V60 pour over targets 400-700 microns, while espresso targets 200-400 microns."
						},
						{
									"@type": "HowToStep",
									"position": 3,
									"name": "Use the texture reference",
									"text": "Match the visual texture analog to calibrate your grinder by feel. Espresso resembles powdered sugar, pour over resembles medium sea salt, and French press resembles raw sugar or peppercorns."
						},
						{
									"@type": "HowToStep",
									"position": 4,
									"name": "Adjust based on taste",
									"text": "If your coffee tastes sour or thin, grind finer (smaller micron number). If it tastes bitter or harsh, grind coarser (larger micron number). Change one click at a time."
						}
			]
})}></script>
	</head>
	<body class="bg-cream">
		<Header />

		<section class="bg-charcoal pt-32 pb-12 md:pb-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
